The built-in "Rathole v2" tunnel (internal/rathole) is a Go reimplementation of
the rathole reverse-proxy protocol by rapiz1 and contributors
(https://github.com/rapiz1/rathole), which is licensed under the Apache License
2.0. No rathole source code is copied; the protocol — its control/data-channel
handshake, message framing, and forwarding design — was reimplemented in Go from
the published specification and source.

The "IP Spoofing" transport (the spoof_* config keys; the spoof carrier in
internal/utils/network/spoof*.go and the KCP integration in kcp.go; the
per-side spoofpipe transports; the spoof tester in internal/spooftest and
internal/manage/spooftest.go) is derived from Backpack by Amin Mohammadi
(AminMGMT) — https://github.com/AminMGMT/backpack — which is licensed under the
GNU Affero General Public License v3.0, the same licence as this project. The
code was ported with attribution under that licence; the tunnel token salts and
module paths were adapted to Arange-tun.
